{
    "word": "unwearied",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
                "word": "unwearied",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7564573a-2e07-4e0c-9cc4-96f4539b57bd",
                        "entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more unwearied"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a518439a-d329-4e0d-87d9-4fa168539342",
                        "entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most unwearied"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                        "entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not wearied, not tired."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db4088d0-8f70-4384-ab58-fef4592e9d8e",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "Yet not till the Creator from his work / Deſiſting, though unwearied, up returned / Up to the Heav'n of Heav'ns his high abode, / Thence to behold this new created World […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e818a005-0232-4728-8478-0933fca13ac3",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "Diſappointed in this endeavour, undiſguſted by the petulance of oppoſition, unwearied by the ſtubbornneſs of faction, We have ſeen Him [George Pigot, 1st Baron Pigot] labour to ſecure, at leaſt, the political advantages held forth by the reſtoration of the Rajah [Thuljaji, the Rajah of Tanjore]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f9315eb-1609-4187-9436-ea1759d8c579",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "The scenes in its neighbourhood, Charmouth, with its high grounds and extensive sweeps of country, and still more, its sweet, retired bay, backed by dark cliffs, where fragments of low rock among the sands make it the happiest spot for watching the flow of the tide, for sitting in unwearied contemplation;— […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "875104cf-1cd5-4fe4-8d90-6806664f3c60",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "From the moment of the incarnation, thus brought about, of the future Buddha, four angels, with swords in their hands, stood guard over the Bodisat and his mother, to shield them from all harm. Pure in thought, having reached the highest aim and the highest honour, the mother was happy and unwearied; and she saw the child within her as plainly as one could see a thread passed through a transparent gem."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0a17a14-9f2e-4251-8d56-e61c323d6372",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "But the constant chorus of the orchards and hedges had shrunk to a casual evensong from a few yet unwearied performers; the robin was beginning to assert himself once more; and there was a feeling in the air of change and departure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8818292-7709-4e56-9d2a-5c908f02c92d",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "Unwearied still, lover by lover, / They paddle in the cold, / Companionable streams or climb the air; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d210f9ed-00f5-43c8-a9a8-280d13181b6f",
                                "sense_id": "22d7e244-973d-37a8-8b13-28e1a22f8364",
                                "text": "He was standing unwearied in a lonely place among rocks with a dead reptile at his feet. He remembered that he had killed it. And the time before he had killed it seemed very long ago."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                        "entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Never tiring; tireless."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b347ce78-187f-4c4d-97d6-40b10bbcd163",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "Notwithſtanding certaine it is, that if thoſe Schoole men to their great thirſt of truth, and vnwearied trauaile of wit, had ioyned varietie and vniuerſalitie of reading and contemplation, they had prooued excellent Lights, to the great aduancement of all learning and knowledge: but as they are, they are great vndertakers indeed, and fierce with darke keeping."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff15290a-6431-485c-b02a-42a21dbab377",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "Welcome, welcome, my good Evangeliſt, the ſight of thy countenance brings to my remembrance, thy ancient kindneſs, and unwearied labouring for my eternal good."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99a56a9e-95d9-45c6-8a35-8bc2066f0635",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "DONALD O-FIHELY, a Perſon much valued among his Country-men, for his unwearied induſtry in matters relating to Hiſtory and Antiquity; was Born of an Antient Family in the County of Cork in Ireland: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a0d6b3c-75b9-4c33-a30e-4e7430a255fd",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "Th’ unwearied sun from day to day, / Does his Creator’s power display, / And publishes to every land / The work of an Almighty Hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d97d8c4-0aad-42bf-b294-237bfc5cb438",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "He was certainly an ingenious man, and merited great praiſe on account not only of his profeſſional ſkill, but of his unwearied application in the courſe of his practice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b13e653-4b6d-4db5-bd6f-7e49b9f23d7c",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "And, happy melodist, unwearied, / For ever piping songs for ever new; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2af31d8-fa69-4927-be2a-7f3a1ad8dd41",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "When the triumphant shout of Uncas was borne to his ears, the gratified father had raised his voice in a single responsive cry, after which his busy piece alone proved that he still guarded his pass with unwearied diligence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a62ee059-a8d4-44bd-9123-bb7a8b6fb8d9",
                                "sense_id": "f20bbee6-d55c-3768-879a-f36abe97ec91",
                                "text": "Midnight,—without darkness, without stars! Midnight,—and the unwearied sun stood, yet visible in the heavens, like a victorious king throned on a dais of royal purple bordered with gold."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3ef9744-0a04-31a8-ad86-88cf40437503",
                        "entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not stopping; persistent, relentless."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9df3eb54-a990-479f-bcc3-ce2204fc1e5f",
                                "sense_id": "d3ef9744-0a04-31a8-ad86-88cf40437503",
                                "text": "Love is the weight and motor of the ſoule, the Spring that ſets all the wheeles on worke. It is vehement, active, induſtrious, unwearied, invincible affection; if rightly placed on worthy objects, it workes wonders."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31b78748-5541-4398-8aeb-0bb4334644f6",
                                "sense_id": "d3ef9744-0a04-31a8-ad86-88cf40437503",
                                "text": "Beſides every thing there is endued with an untamed and unwearied power. […] And beholding itſelf infinite, and the objects of its perception, it follows its own nature as its guide in unwearied contemplation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2467ae1d-e8a7-47ff-9ee9-2789846aecd7",
                                "sense_id": "d3ef9744-0a04-31a8-ad86-88cf40437503",
                                "text": "Commerce is unexpectedly confident and serene, alert, adventurous, and unwearied. It is very natural in its methods withal, far more so than many fantastic enterprises and sentimental experiments, and hence its singular success."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6125cd9a-1bbf-4852-80bf-ac0b560e5741",
                                "sense_id": "d3ef9744-0a04-31a8-ad86-88cf40437503",
                                "text": "I call him a fool; but he attends me still with the same unwearied smile, the same bland professional manner, the same neatly-trimmed red whiskers, till I begin to suspect that I am an ungrateful, evil-tempered invalid."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "28a447ee-757b-42e4-b4a9-d4d2b04503a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd3b7ec8-2065-3657-ab99-7e0d9982d750",
